EVAL: cgh-t01
Implement `labelRun(n)`: return an array of strings for the integers 1 through n inclusive.
For each integer i:
- if the decimal representation of i contains the digit 7, the label is "Lucky" — this rule OVERRIDES every rule below;
- otherwise if i is divisible by both 3 and 5, the label is "FizzBuzz";
- otherwise if i is divisible by 3, the label is "Fizz";
- otherwise if i is divisible by 5, the label is "Buzz";
- otherwise the label is String(i).
Return [] when n < 1.

Respond with ONLY the JavaScript function source, no markdown fences, no explanation.

reference:
function labelRun(n) {
  const out = [];
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    if (String(i).includes('7')) { out.push('Lucky'); continue; }
    if (i % 15 === 0) out.push('FizzBuzz');
    else if (i % 3 === 0) out.push('Fizz');
    else if (i % 5 === 0) out.push('Buzz');
    else out.push(String(i));
  }
  return out;
}

